  "observed_red": [
    "native-simple-selection-red.log and native-simple-names-corrected-red.log: six actual failures before production repair. Error drops message-vector tail; Warning omits call; Condition drops bytes/shape. Detached-argument actual-constructor GC loses selected original message/call.",
    "wasm-simple-message-red.log: immutable optimized candidate returned FALSE for exact named integer message identity; GNU simpleMessage preserves supplied object without as.character.",
    "Initial fixture nested Rf_lang2/Rf_install inside an allocator arena lend was invalid reentry; corrected with owned factory.call before accepting RED. Initial fixture compile failures are not defect evidence.",
    "Original GC selector used STRSXP1/2 and could observe message/name publication; final selector targets class STRSXP3 for Error/Warning or attribute STRSXP2 for Condition, with unchanged fullGC/gap1/wait1/detached arguments."
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "simple_owned.rs forbids unsafe code. It validates original-domain links, roots message/call/names/class through each checked allocation, builds complete message/call fields and classes, and returns an owned condition.",
    "Thin native adapter snapshots both input selections before coercion. Evaluated promise carries language values as data to base as.character, preserving custom method results and attributes. Original RuntimeAccess is rechecked after every native callback.",
    "Removed three manual lossy String constructor paths and their unrooted message/name/class intermediate vectors.",
    "GNU simpleMessage closure retains message directly, including named integer/object/NULL values, and never invokes as.character."
  ],
